{"result":"{
  "metadata": {
    "id": "482345007",
    "title": "04.4.6 VIC Exclusive — Merchandiser Working Guide",
    "type": "page",
    "created": "",
    "updated": "",
    "url": "https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/SFCC/pages/482345007",
    "space": {
      "key": "SFCC",
      "name": "Adobe SFCC"
    },
    "version": 2,
    "attachments": [],
    "content": {
      "value": "overviewOverview\n----------------\n\nVIC Exclusive is a product visibility mechanism that allows Zimmermann to restrict certain products to VIC customers only, while still making them purchasable by anyone with a direct URL. On average, 6–8 styles per season are designated VIC Exclusive.\n\nThis guide explains how merchandisers set up and manage VIC Exclusive products end-to-end, across Business Manager, badge configuration, and the VIC landing page.\n\n---\n\nhow-it-works--summaryHow it works — Summary\n-------------------------------------------\n\nVIC Exclusive operates across three layers:\n\n| Layer | What it does |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Product flag** | Controls product visibility on category listings and site search |\n| **Badge category** | A non-navigational SFCC category that groups all VIC Exclusive products across seasons, used to surface the VIC Exclusive badge on PDP and PLP |\n| **Landing page & season PLPs** | A public-facing page (accessible via private token-based URL) that links out to season-specific PLPs, each backed by a dedicated VIC Exclusive season category |\n\n---\n\nstep-1--flag-a-product-as-vic-exclusive-in-business-managerStep 1 — Flag a product as VIC Exclusive in Business Manager\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nTo mark a product as VIC Exclusive:\n\n1. Open the product in **Business Manager → Merchant Tools → Products**\n2. Locate the custom attribute `isVICExclusive`\n3. Set the value to **true**\n4. Save the product\n\nThe flag is applied on the next search index — no republishing or recreation of the product is required.\n\n**What this does:**\n\n* The product is **hidden** from category listings and site search for any customer not in the VIC customer group\n* The product remains **visible** to VIC customers browsing normally (shown with the VIC Exclusive badge)\n* The product's PDP remains **accessible to anyone** with a direct URL, regardless of login state\n* The product is **excluded from search engine indexing** and Google Shopping feeds\n\n**To reverse VIC Exclusive status:** set `isVICExclusive` to **false** and save. The product returns to normal visibility on the next index.\n\n---\n\nstep-2--assign-the-product-to-the-vic-exclusive-badge-categoryStep 2 — Assign the product to the VIC Exclusive badge category\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nThe VIC Exclusive badge category is a single, non-navigational category in SFCC that groups all VIC Exclusive products across all seasons. It does not appear as a navigation category on the storefront — its sole purpose is to trigger the VIC Exclusive badge on PDP and PLP.\n\nTo assign the badge:\n\n1. Open the product in Business Manager\n2. Navigate to the **Categories** tab\n3. Assign the product to the **VIC Exclusive** badge category\n4. Save\n\nWhen a shopper clicks the VIC Exclusive badge on the PDP, they are navigated to the VIC Exclusive badge category PLP URL.\n\n**To remove the badge:** remove the product from the badge category in Business Manager. The badge will no longer appear on the PDP or PLP.\n\n---\n\nstep-3--set-up-a-vic-exclusive-season-categoryStep 3 — Set up a VIC Exclusive season category\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nIn addition to the badge category, each season's VIC Exclusive products should be assigned to a dedicated season category. This category powers the PLP that the VIC landing page links out to, allowing shoppers to browse that season's exclusive styles.\n\n**Suggested naming convention:** VIC Exclusive — [Season] [Year] *(e.g. VIC Exclusive — Resort 2027)*\n\nTo set up a season category:\n\n1. Create a new category in Business Manager under the appropriate catalogue\n2. Name it according to the convention above\n3. Assign all VIC Exclusive products for that season to this category\n4. Note the category PLP URL — this will be used when configuring the landing page\n\n---\n\nstep-4--configure-the-vic-exclusive-landing-pageStep 4 — Configure the VIC Exclusive landing page\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nThe VIC Exclusive landing page is a public-facing page accessible via a private token-based URL ([SFCC-629](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-629)). Customers do not need to be logged in or assigned to the VIC customer group to access it via this URL.\n\nThe landing page links out to each season's VIC Exclusive PLP. To add or update a season link:\n\n1. Navigate to the VIC Exclusive landing page configuration in Contentful\n2. Add or update the link pointing to the relevant season category PLP URL (configured in Step 3)\n3. Publish the entry\n\nEach season link on the landing page should correspond to an active VIC Exclusive season category with products assigned.\n\n---\n\nendtoend-checklistEnd-to-end checklist\n--------------------------------------\n\nUse this checklist at the start of each VIC Exclusive season drop:\n\n* [ ] Flag each VIC Exclusive product with `isVICExclusive = true` in Business Manager\n* [ ] Assign each product to the **VIC Exclusive badge category**\n* [ ] Create a new **VIC Exclusive season category** (e.g. VIC Exclusive — Resort 2027)\n* [ ] Assign all season products to the season category\n* [ ] Note the season category PLP URL\n* [ ] Update the VIC Exclusive landing page in Contentful with the new season link\n* [ ] Publish the landing page entry\n* [ ] Verify the PLP is accessible via direct URL\n* [ ] Verify the VIC Exclusive badge is rendering correctly on PDP and PLP\n\n---\n\nremoving-vic-exclusive-statusRemoving VIC Exclusive status\n----------------------------------------------------------\n\nWhen a product moves from VIC Exclusive to general availability:\n\n1. Set `isVICExclusive` to **false** in Business Manager and save — the product returns to normal visibility on the next index\n2. Remove the product from the **VIC Exclusive badge category** — the badge will no longer render\n3. Decide whether to keep the product in the season category (it will remain accessible on that PLP)\n\n---\n\nrelated-user-storiesRelated user stories\n----------------------------------------\n\n* [SFCC-303 — VIC Exclusive Product Visibility](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-303)\n* [SFCC-225 — PDP Product Badges — Merchandiser Configuration](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-225)\n* [SFCC-629 — Loyalty: Private VIC Marketing URL Access](https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/browse/SFCC-629)",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "emoji": "1f451",
    "page_width": "fixed-width"
  }
}"}

